        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This updates the Express Tutorial to v5</p>
<p dir="auto">I wrote some tests in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3210853343" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/express-locallibrary-tutorial/issues/327" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/express-locallibrary-tutorial/pull/327/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/express-locallibrary-tutorial/pull/327">mdn/express-locallibrary-tutorial#327</a>, then updated Express to v5 along with all dependencies - everything passed. Then ran all the code mods (<code class="notranslate">npx @expressjs/codemod upgrade</code>) suggested in the <a href="https://expressjs.com/en/guide/migrating-5.html" rel="nofollow">migration guide</a> - nothing was changed. So I don't think I was using anything impacted by a changed or removed API.</p>
<p dir="auto">What I do need to do though is remove my code to do async error handling in routes, since that is now handled automatically. I also want to update the structure of where mongoose is added to match the tests. The way it was done in the app.js means that tests can't work (because you can't have multiple connections, and if you do this in the app there is already a connection by the time you get to the test runner).</p>
<p dir="auto">Actions:</p>
<ul class="contains-task-list">
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" id="" disabled="" class="task-list-item-checkbox" aria-label="Completed task" checked=""> Fix up all links from 4x to 5x</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" id="" disabled="" class="task-list-item-checkbox" aria-label="Incomplete task"> Fix up the mongoose instructions to set up the tests in the bin/www file.</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" id="" disabled="" class="task-list-item-checkbox" aria-label="Incomplete task"> Fix up later instructions that update the DB url so that they point to www.</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" id="" disabled="" class="task-list-item-checkbox" aria-label="Completed task" checked=""> Fix up environment instructions to match current LTS versions of node etc.</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" id="" disabled="" class="task-list-item-checkbox" aria-label="Completed task" checked=""> Fix up all dependencies.</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" id="" disabled="" class="task-list-item-checkbox" aria-label="Incomplete task"> Remove v4 patch for hacking async error handling</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" id="" disabled="" class="task-list-item-checkbox" aria-label="Incomplete task"> Work through and tidy up docs.</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" id="" disabled="" class="task-list-item-checkbox" aria-label="Incomplete task"> <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Extensions/Server-side/Express_Nodejs/routes#route_paths" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Extensions/Server-side/Express_Nodejs/routes#route_paths</a> - I think this changed. Check in path route matching syntax in <a href="https://expressjs.com/en/guide/migrating-5.html#res.send.status" rel="nofollow">https://expressjs.com/en/guide/migrating-5.html#res.send.status</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #38922.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2964520362" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38922" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/38922/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38922">#38922</a></p>]]></content>
